 ### A-NeRF Baseline Configuration
-Use a bigger foreground mask for ray sampling. Enable background estimation in the official code. Use L2 loss instead of L1 loss [S10]. A-NeRF uses only keypoints instead of surface models to construct conditional inputs to NeRF networks, making it easy to confuse background and foreground, resulting in floating blob artifacts [S10]. A-NeRF cannot generalize to unseen poses when training poses are limited, yielding the worst generalization results among baselines on ZJU-MoCap [S10].
